<section class="section privacy-section" id="privacy">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-heading split-heading reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow privacy-eyebrow"><span></span>Private by architecture</p>
        <h2>Your voice stays local by default.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Privacy is a mode you can see, not a promise hidden in a policy. Local
        Transcription is the default; every network path requires a choice from you.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-console reveal">
      <div class="privacy-console-head">
        <span>Data path / Local Transcription</span>
        <strong><i></i> On-device route active</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="local-flow" aria-label="Local transcription data flow">
        <div class="flow-node">
          <span class="flow-index">01</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="11" rx="3"/><path d="M5 11a7 7 0 0 0 14 0M12 18v3"/></svg>
          <div><strong>Your voice</strong><small>Captured only while recording</small></div>
        </div>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="flow-node flow-node-active">
          <span class="flow-index">02</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 19v2m8-2v2M9 9h6m-6 4h3"/></svg>
          <div><strong>Local transcription</strong><small>faster-whisper on your PC</small></div>
          <em>Audio stays here</em>
        </div>
        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="flow-node">
          <span class="flow-index">03</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 5h14M5 10h14M5 15h9"/><path d="m16 17 2 2 4-5"/></svg>
          <div><strong>Clean text</strong><small>Pasted at your cursor</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="optional-routes">
        <article>
          <div class="route-title"><span>Optional route A</span><strong>Cloud Transcription</strong></div>
          <p>Audio is sent to the transcription provider you configure only after you explicitly select Cloud mode.</p>
          <small>Off by default · Uses your provider choice</small>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="route-title"><span>Optional route B</span><strong>Pro Mode</strong></div>
          <p>After transcription, finished text—not audio—is sent to the AI provider you configure for polish or presets.</p>
          <small>Optional · Uses your own key</small>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-details">
      <article class="privacy-statement reveal">
        <span class="statement-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</span>
        <blockquote>No account required. No telemetry. No required cloud.</blockquote>
        <p>
          Local mode works offline after setup. Short dictation buffers are discarded
          after transcription; meeting recordings stay on your device until you delete them.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><span></span>No usage analytics or tracking</li>
          <li><span></span>Keys are stored only on your machine</li>
          <li><span></span>MIT licensed · public repository link pending</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="provider-panel reveal delay-1">
        <p class="card-index">Your AI / Your choice</p>
        <h3>Connect a provider—or none at all.</h3>
        <p>Pro Mode supports your own keys and local models. External providers may have their own usage costs.</p>
        <div class="provider-list" aria-label="Supported AI back-ends">
          <span>Cerebras</span><span>OpenAI</span><span>Anthropic</span>
          <span>DeepSeek</span><span>Groq</span><span>OpenRouter</span><span class="provider-local">Local</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-foot"><i></i> Mumble never supplies or shares a built-in key.</div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
